  "notes": [
    "upstream: rodrgo/expander-sae@598f59a (MIT); SAE classes and training loop imported unmodified; the Modal orchestration is replaced by a local driver that follows experiments/scaling_qwen2_5_3b.py stage by stage; file hashes scaling_qwen2_5_3b.py 8ccc61adf149, expander.py 6678e40dc160, dense.py 42c5eb3df18b, training.py 0c6619878406, qwen2_5_3b_replication.json dab2ac7024ba",
    "data: monology/pile-uncopyrighted at revision 3be90335b66f, first 6000 documents cached (sha256 d51839c0a70e); base corpus = the first 2400 documents, extracted in order and truncated to 200000 training + 5000 test tokens (upstream's 205k tokens end near document 1680; the rest is slack for the bootstrap axis); the 'later slice' corpus starts at document 2500; held-out evaluation uses documents from 5000 on, which no training corpus in this battery touches",
    "reproduction: shipped layer-12 CE-recovered (0.833, 0.827, 0.825) (expander d=7) and (0.983, 0.983, 0.982) (dense warm-tied), ratio 0.842; base run here 0.831 and 0.978, ratio 0.850 (bf16 on a different GPU and torch; exact byte reproduction is not expected)",
    "denominators in the base run: CE_clean 2.290, CE_zero-ablated 15.987 nats/token, so 'CE recovered' is measured against a 13.7-nat collapse; the mean-ablation and held-out runs in the hyperparams axis show what the same dictionaries retain under the other convention and on text they were not trained on",
    "evaluation overlap in the upstream protocol: the 100 CE-evaluation sequences are the first 100 documents of the stream, and the training pool is the first ~205k tokens of the same stream, so upstream's CE recovered is measured on training text; the 'eval_set=held-out' run is the same protocol on unseen documents",
    "no null control: the finding has no component set, so no specificity ratio can be formed; the substantive comparison is between measurement conventions, reported per run in the manifest",
    "v0.3 grade: A; regraded 2026-09-03 under grade rule v0.4 from the recorded checks (schema 0.5)"
  ],
